{"id":"4e0c4931e04834e5","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy.md","title":"Ideal Completeness Hierarchy","display":"thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy — Ideal Completeness Hierarchy","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy","aliases":["58-thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy"],"display":"thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy — Ideal Completeness Hierarchy","depends_on":["[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[58-df-zfc-card6-cardinal-lt]]","[[58-df-equinumerous]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-ideal-completeness-hierarchy — Ideal Completeness Hierarchy"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"86c688a672128b44\" href=\"?note=86c688a672128b44\" title=\"58-df-zfc-card6-cardinal-lt\">58-df-zfc-card6-cardinal-lt</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"28c79fde9f892bfe\" href=\"?note=28c79fde9f892bfe\" title=\"58-df-equinumerous\">58-df-equinumerous</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I,X,\\kappa,\\lambda,\\mathcal A\\in V\">\\(I,X,\\kappa,\\lambda,\\mathcal A\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CardinalLt}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CardinalLt}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\\)</span> are the exact cardinal predicates.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IdealCompletenessNumber}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{IdealCompletenessNumber}_S\\)</span> are defined below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}set\\text{-}ideal}\\vdash \\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\leftrightarrow I\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\\land\\varnothing\\in I\\land X\\notin I\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\{x\\}\\in I)\\land\\forall A\\in I\\;\\forall B\\subseteq A\\;(B\\in I)\\land\\forall A,B\\in I\\;(A\\cup B\\in I).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}set\\text{-}ideal}\\vdash \\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\leftrightarrow I\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\\land\\varnothing\\in I\\land X\\notin I\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\{x\\}\\in I)\\land\\forall A\\in I\\;\\forall B\\subseteq A\\;(B\\in I)\\land\\forall A,B\\in I\\;(A\\cup B\\in I).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}kappa\\text{-}complete}\\vdash \\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\mathcal A\\subseteq I\\;(\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CardinalLt}_S(\\mathcal A,\\kappa)\\to\\bigcup\\mathcal A\\in I).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}kappa\\text{-}complete}\\vdash \\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\mathcal A\\subseteq I\\;(\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CardinalLt}_S(\\mathcal A,\\kappa)\\to\\bigcup\\mathcal A\\in I).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}definition}\\vdash \\mathrm{IdealCompletenessNumber}_S(c,I,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(c)\\land\\exists\\mathcal A\\subseteq I\\;(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(\\mathcal A,c)\\land\\bigcup\\mathcal A\\notin I)\\land\\forall\\mathcal B\\subseteq I\\;(\\bigcup\\mathcal B\\notin I\\to\\neg\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CardinalLt}_S(\\mathcal B,c)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}definition}\\vdash \\mathrm{IdealCompletenessNumber}_S(c,I,X)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(c)\\land\\exists\\mathcal A\\subseteq I\\;(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(\\mathcal A,c)\\land\\bigcup\\mathcal A\\notin I)\\land\\forall\\mathcal B\\subseteq I\\;(\\bigcup\\mathcal B\\notin I\\to\\neg\\mathrm{ZfcCard6CardinalLt}_S(\\mathcal B,c)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}hierarchy}\\vdash \\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land\\kappa\\leq\\lambda\\land\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\lambda)\\to\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\kappa).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}hierarchy}\\vdash \\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\lambda)\\land\\kappa\\leq\\lambda\\land\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\lambda)\\to\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\kappa).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}threshold}\\vdash \\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\to\\left(\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\\exists c\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{IdealCompletenessNumber}_S(c,I,X)\\land\\kappa\\leq c)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}threshold}\\vdash \\mathrm{SetIdeal}_S(I,X)\\land\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\to\\left(\\mathrm{KappaCompleteIdeal}_S(I,X,\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow\\exists c\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{IdealCompletenessNumber}_S(c,I,X)\\land\\kappa\\leq c)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Completeness is monotone downward in the cardinal parameter, and the relational completeness number is the first cardinal size at which closure under unions can fail.</li>\n<li>For regular uncountable <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>, the nonstationary ideal <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NS}_\\kappa\">\\(\\mathrm{NS}_\\kappa\\)</span> is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-complete but not <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa^+\">\\(\\kappa^+\\)</span>-complete, so <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{comp}(\\mathrm{NS}_\\kappa)=\\kappa\">\\(\\operatorname{comp}(\\mathrm{NS}_\\kappa)=\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-1